  ── HOW TO RETIRE AN ASK once you have done it on a device
     Put the date on the SAME line as the marker, then commit:
       // NEEDS-FOUNDER-VERIFY VERIFIED-YYYY-MM-DD: <the original instruction>
     Keep the instruction. The line stays as the record of WHAT was confirmed and
       WHEN — deleting it also deletes the date, which is the first thing you want
       back when the behaviour regresses.
  
  ── LIMITS (read before treating this as a work queue)
     ANSWERED depends on somebody writing the mark. An ask you did on a device but
       never marked stays in the open list — the tool reads the tree, not your
       memory. It fails toward noise on purpose: a half-typed mark leaves the ask
       OPEN, because showing a settled ask costs a glance and hiding an open one
       costs a device session.
     The AREA is derived from the file path, never from the words. A layout ask living in a
       bio file lands under 'bio'. Order the walk yourself; this only makes the queue visible.
     It reads RAW text on purpose — every marker is a comment.
     The NOT-ASKS split keys on a determiner in front of the marker, and can only
       REMOVE from the list above. A sentence about the backlog phrased without one
       stays counted as an ask — noise, never a hidden job.
     BLOCKED is a HAND-WRITTEN mark, not a derivation. Nothing here can tell that a
       door was removed; somebody has to notice and write BLOCKED-BY-#<slice> on the
       marker line. So this list under-reports: an ask whose door died unnoticed is
       still shown as open, which is the safe direction and not a clean bill.

